{"id": "tea:nyayapravesa:1", "source": "src:nyayapravesa", "location": {"ref": "1"}, "paraphrase": "Proof and refutation, with their fallacies, serve to convince others; perception and inference, with their fallacies, serve one's own understanding.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["dispute"], "concepts": ["cpt:trairupya"], "teachers": ["tch:sankarasvamin"], "notes": "Opening verse recalled.", "coverage": ["B4", "D"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U41-yogacara-pramana"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U41-yogacara-pramana"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:nyayapravesa:2", "source": "src:nyayapravesa", "location": {"ref": "2"}, "paraphrase": "The reason has three aspects: it is a property of the subject, present in similar cases and absent from dissimilar cases; the thesis, reason and example with their fallacies (e.g. 'sound is eternal' contradicted by perception or by common knowledge) are enumerated.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["dispute"], "terms": ["trm:trairupya", "trm:hetvabhasa"], "teachers": ["tch:sankarasvamin"], "notes": "Section-level summary.", "coverage": ["B4", "D"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U41-yogacara-pramana"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U41-yogacara-pramana"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
